  For the longest time I was a big champion of the Valkyrie
character. I've ascended a few of them and have always felt that their
ability to rapidly gain hit points along with the benefit of gaining
Mjollnir made them the toughest. Well...

 Around 2 weeks ago I started my first ever Samurai - and ascended him!
I know, it was hardly due to my "abilities" that he made it so
far (one could even say "in spite of" my abilities); mainly beautiful
luck and nice breaks. But I'm hooked on them now. They also gain
hit points rapidly and a juiced up (+6) Tsurugi is pretty powerful
in its own right. Plus their quest is also nice in that it has the
supply rooms. 

  Anyway, as is usually the case, the key points of whether or not
my character would survive occurred in the Mines. Having to waste
alot of time moving stuff around due to finding zero bags of holding
in the mine town or elsewhere, I ran into around 15 Uruk-hais down
a couple of levels below the town. Only by reading an unidentified
spellbook and being teleported randomly was I able to survive.
Not yet having poison resistance made them all the more dangerous.
Running back up a flight, I discovered a scroll of genocide and thus
took care of 'o's. The major coup however was discovering 
a wand of wishing a couple of levels down. (The first time I've ever
found one outside of the castle). With that I wished for the all-important
reflection and thus could really begin sailing...
